N1  - <p>BOINC criterion evidence - Introduction, verbatim: "There exists a number of classes of computationally intense geoacoustic inversion problems, which can be solved using embarrassing parallelism. This is the main reason why we launched the volunteer computing project Acoustics@home, aimed at solving such problems. The project is based on the popular platform BOINC (Berkley Open Infrastructure for Network Compuitng [3])." | Full text: Open Engineering 7(1):363-370 (2017) | Link: Acoustics@home / BOINC | Source: Open Engineering (2017)ER&nbsp;&nbsp;-</p>
